    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41524" root="وأب" body-key="w">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأَبَ</span></b> , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَئِبُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأْبَةٌ</span> [app. a mistake
for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأْبٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبَةٌ</span>], <i>It</i> (a hoof) <i>was contracted in
its edges,</i> or <i>in its fore edges.</i> (Az.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأْبٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأَبَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَئِبُ</span>, (S, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأْبٌ</span> (S) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبَةٌ</span>
(S, K) <i>He contracted himself,</i> or <i>drew himself
together,</i> or <i>shrank; and was ashamed.</i> (S, K.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأَبَ</span> (TA) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اٰتَّأَبَ</span></b>  (S, K) <i>He was ashamed,</i>
(S, K,) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْ شَىْءٍ</span> <i>of a thing.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَأَبَ</span>, aor.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَئِبُ</span>, <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انف</span> [app. meaning <i>He was disdainful</i>].
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَئِبَ</span>, [aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَوْءَبُ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَطِئَ</span>:] <i>He was
angry.</i> (K.)

